KZ2 6086: guest-validate (patch 2017) skips its band-hash pass when patch 6077's write watch says nothing wrote the
surface's guest span (LD_GV_WW=1, off by default; no change in what is drawn: a skip is taken only where the hashes
would come out the same).
ld_gv_hash_bands re-reads the guest bytes under every live colour surface, as a baseline after the GPU's writes and as
a compare at most once a frame when the surface is bound as a texture. In the Corinth Sands fight on 0.1.13 that is
~7-9 MB and 1.3-1.9 ms a frame on the frame thread ([guest-validate]: about 18 baselines and 4 checks a frame), with
uploads=0 for the whole run (also in The New Sun and at a Continue checkpoint in Corinth River). A 4-lane hash made
no difference (+0.5 %, ranges overlap): the pass is bound by memory, not by the hash.
With the switch, the pass first asks the write watch (ld_ww_skip_or_arm, new in rsx_tex_ww.h: collect the span, then
"clean since this surface's arm, and the geometry the hashes were made with is unchanged" = skip; otherwise arm and
hash as before, the arm taken before the bytes are read). New (empty) band hashes, a moved or resized surface, a
written page or a failed query all hash. Spans outside the watched guest space never take part. Hashing falls to
~36 us a frame; [guest-validate] gains ww-skips=N.
Measured (native Windows, Ryzen 9 9950X3D, RTX 4090; unattended Corinth Sands, 120 s runs, on top of patch 6085 and a
PGO build): 46.80 +- 0.74 -> 48.29 +- 2.80 over three rounds (one run disturbed), 45.39 +- 5.33 -> 48.65 +- 2.82 over
four (two rounds disturbed on every variant, the baseline too); the two clean rounds 48.1 / 49.3 -> 51.05 / 51.12
(issue #102).
Not checked: a scene where guest-validate does upload (none found in the first level), Proton, LD_TEX_WW=2 (verify
mode: the switch stays out of the way there).
Host test: tools/runtime/test_gv_write_watch.sh (the real function on a fake write watch: a random run against
"hash every time", shared pages, a failed query, a negative control; and the wiring).
Upstream candidate together with 6077 (ps3recomp libs/video/rsx_live_draw.c, rsx_tex_ww.h).

